This is a complete implementation of the custom web component using ES Modules and Shadow DOM.

### `x-details.js`

```javascript
/**
 * Custom Web Component: <x-details>
 * Provides functionality similar to the <details> element, but always shows an "intro" part when collapsed.
 */
class XDetails extends HTMLElement {
    constructor() {
        super();
        // 1. Create and attach the Shadow DOM
        this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' });
        this.isExpanded = false;

        // 2. Create the internal structure (template)
        this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `
            <style>
                :host {
                    display: block;
                    border: 1px solid #ccc;
                    border-radius: 4px;
                    margin: 10px 0;
                    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
                    background-color: #f9f9f9;
                }

                .details-container {
                    padding: 15px;
                    box-sizing: border-box;
                }

                /* Header Styling */
                .header-bar {
                    display: flex;
                    align-items: center;
                    cursor: pointer;
                    padding-bottom: 10px;
                    border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
                    margin-bottom: 10px;
                    font-size: 1.2em; /* Slightly larger font */
                    font-weight: bold;
                    color: #333;
                }

                .toggle-icon {
                    font-size: 1.2em;
                    margin-right: 10px;
                    transition: transform 0.3s;
                }

                /* Content sections */
                .intro-content {
                    margin-bottom: 15px;
                    padding: 10px 0;
                }

                .details-content {
                    max-height: 0;
                    overflow: hidden;
                    transition: max-height 0.3s ease-out;
                    padding-top: 10px;
                    padding-bottom: 15px;
                }

                .details-content.expanded {
                    max-height: 500px; /* Must be larger than content height */
                }

                /* Button Styling */
                .expand-button {
                    background-color: #007bff;
                    color: white;
                    border: none;
                    padding: 8px 15px;
                    cursor: pointer;
                    border-radius: 4px;
                    font-size: 1em;
                    transition: background-color 0.2s;
                }

                .expand-button:hover {
                    background-color: #0056b3;
                }
            </style>

            <div class="details-container">
                <div class="header-bar" role="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="details-content">
                    <span class="toggle-icon" id="toggle-icon">+</span>
                    <slot name="header"></slot>
                </div>

                <div class="intro-content">
                    <slot name="intro"></slot>
                </div>

                <!-- Details section that can be hidden -->
                <div class="details-content" id="details-content">
                    <slot name="details"></slot>
                </div>

                <!-- Expand button placeholder (only shown when collapsed) -->
                <button class="expand-button" id="expand-button" style="display: none;">Expand more</button>
            </div>
        `;
    }

    connectedCallback() {
        // 3. Get references to elements
        const headerBar = this.shadowRoot.querySelector('.header-bar');
        const detailsContent = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('details-content');
        const toggleIcon = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('toggle-icon');
        const expandButton = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('expand-button');

        // 4. Initial setup
        this._updateUI();

        // 5. Event listener for the header (toggle action)
        headerBar.addEventListener('click', () => this.toggle());

        // 6. Event listener for the expand button (toggle action)
        expandButton.addEventListener('click', () => this.toggle());
    }

    /**
     * Toggles the expanded state and updates the UI.
     */
    toggle() {
        this.isExpanded = !this.isExpanded;
        this._updateUI();
    }

    /**
     * Updates the visual state (icons, height, button visibility).
     * @private
     */
    _updateUI() {
        const detailsContent = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('details-content');
        const toggleIcon = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('toggle-icon');
        const expandButton = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('expand-button');
        const headerBar = this.shadowRoot.querySelector('.header-bar');

        if (this.isExpanded) {
            // Expanded state
            detailsContent.classList.add('expanded');
            toggleIcon.textContent = '–'; // Minus sign
            headerBar.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
            expandButton.style.display = 'none';
        } else {
            // Collapsed state
            detailsContent.classList.remove('expanded');
            toggleIcon.textContent = '+'; // Plus sign
            headerBar.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
            expandButton.style.display = 'block';
        }
    }
}

// 7. Define the custom element
customElements.define('x-details', XDetails);
```

### How to Use It (HTML)

To run this component, you need to include the JavaScript file.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>X-Details Component Demo</title>
    <!-- Import the component script -->
    <script src="x-details.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Custom X-Details Component Demo</h1>

    <!-- EXAMPLE 1: Standard Usage -->
    <x-details>
      <!-- Content for slot="header" -->
      <span slot="header">Detailed Project Summary</span>

      <!-- Content for slot="intro" (always visible) -->
      <div slot="intro">
        <strong>Overview:</strong> This project aims to demonstrate how custom web components can enhance native HTML elements by adding custom behavior and structure. The intro part is always visible regardless of expansion state.
      </div>

      <!-- Content for slot="details" (hidden when collapsed) -->
      <div slot="details">
        <h2>Technical Details</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Web Components API used (CustomElements)</li>
            <li>Styling contained via Shadow DOM</li>
            <li>Toggle logic managed by JavaScript</li>
            <li>Intro content persists when collapsed</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </x-details>

    <hr>

    <!-- EXAMPLE 2: Minimal Usage -->
    <x-details>
      <span slot="header">Quick Tips</span>
      <div slot="intro">Remember to check the documentation for advanced usage!</div>
      <div slot="details">Remember to close all files before saving, otherwise your browser might struggle.</div>
    </x-details>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation of Features

1.  **Shadow DOM Encapsulation:** All styles (CSS) and internal structure are isolated within the Shadow Root, preventing leakage and ensuring the component looks consistent regardless of the host page's styling.
2.  **Slots:** `slot="header"`, `slot="intro"`, and `slot="details"` allow the user to inject content into specific, predefined areas of the component.
3.  **Always Visible Intro:** The `intro-content` section is rendered outside the expandable details content, fulfilling the core requirement.
4.  **Toggling Mechanism:** The `toggle()` method manages the `isExpanded` state.
5.  **CSS Transition:** Using `max-height: 0` and the `expanded` class allows the details section to smoothly transition (slide) open and closed.
6.  **User Interaction:** The component allows the user to click either the header or the dedicated "Expand more" button to trigger the expansion.
7.  **Visual Indicators:** The `+` and `–` icons dynamically update to show the current state.

